chunks.text:
## Test Cases and Scenarios
1. Automated (Vitest):
encryption/decryption roundtrip + bad key behavior;
webhook secret verification and constant-time compare path;
GitLab hook upsert logic (create vs update existing URL);
delivery dedup with repeated same event UUID;
event filtering (branch push yes, tag push no, MR action allowlist);
retry scheduling/backoff and terminal dead-letter behavior;
disconnect semantics (unlink vs last-member full disable).
2. Route-level integration tests:
connect new project success;
connect existing integration links membership and enqueues verify job;
webhook ingest unauthorized token rejected;
webhook ingest valid token enqueues exactly one job;
runner processes pending jobs and writes result.
3. Manual QA:
onboarding with valid token provisions hook and continues;
onboarding with forced hook failure shows warning but allows continue;
settings shows status + allows resync/rotate/unlink;
cron-triggered runner drains queue and retries transient failures.

## Rollout and Monitoring
1. Deploy migration before enabling UI actions.
2. Configure scheduler:
`/api/internal/gitlab-jobs/run` every minute,
`/api/internal/gitlab-jobs/cleanup` daily.
3. Add structured logs for connect/resync/disconnect/webhook ingest/runner outcomes.
4. Track health via counts:
pending/failed/dead jobs, webhook rejects, hook sync failures.

